# T15 integration boundary — minimal owning-module implementation required
# Worker base: 0b8a7526db58b7a296ead5f98d1d13a5c10b86ff
# No source changes outside the T15 allocation are made here.

The assigned test/docs files cannot supply a real end-to-end UI because the integrated
web application does not implement the API-backed login/project/media/editor workflow:

- `apps/web/src/app/routes.tsx` mounts only `Workbench`.
- `apps/web/src/features/projects/Projects.tsx` explicitly marks itself DEV MOCK and
  offers a static project card only.
- `apps/web/src/features/workbench/Workbench.tsx` owns a fixed fixture ontology and
  generated fixture object list; it does not consume project/media/annotation APIs.
- `AttributePanel.tsx` renders disabled/readOnly inputs. CanvasView has a real T09
  renderer component, but Workbench does not construct an EditorAssetRequest or mount it.
- The configured Playwright webServer (`scripts/serve-wgpu-probe.mjs`) serves only the
  WebGPU probe, not the application. The WebGPU project therefore has no authenticated
  real UI surface for the T15 browser fixture to exercise.

Required parent-owned cutover (do not merge this prose as a code diff):

1. Add the actual session UI and project creation/list API flows in the existing app
   shell/features. Project creation and asset import must call the authenticated public
   endpoints, with cookie/CSRF and user-visible errors; do not retain the DEV MOCK card.
2. Replace Workbench fixture state with API-backed project, ontology, asset list, head
   annotation and canonical image data. Mount CanvasView with the selected MediaRevision,
   ontology, document and canonical RGBA; use EditorHost's real WebGPU `gpu-status`
   diagnostics. Connect the existing real toolbar/attribute/object components to editor
   deltas without a second mutable geometry owner.
3. Wire the existing persistence SaveQueue / SaveStatus to the API and persist changed
   documents. Add explicit confirmed-negative UI confirmation before `set_completion`,
   and reject/disable confirmation while objects remain. Keep completion distinct from
   empty/unprocessed.
4. Connect actual T14 revision-bound export UI: save/flush, use the resulting immutable
   annotation revision, POST `/api/annotation-revisions/{id}/exports` with COCO loss
   acknowledgement, GET the authenticated download, and expose bytes as a browser
   download. Never assert only the filename or the visible label.
5. Serve the real web app and API in the `chromium-webgpu` test environment and perform
   actual login through the UI. Preserve real GPU enforcement; do not stub WebGPU,
   mock API traffic, use editor-internal command shortcuts, or relax project isolation.

After that owned implementation exists, keep `tests/e2e/t15_vertical.spec.ts` as the
public acceptance contract, adapt only selectors to the actual shipped surface, and run
`pnpm test:task T15` with the real hardware adapter. This assignment cannot implement
or verify those cross-module items under its explicit file allocation.
